Article 1: The conduct prescribed in Article 338 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China, under any of the following circumstances, shall be deemed as "seriously polluting the environment":
(1) discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing infectious disease pathogens, or toxic substances within the primary protection zone of drinking water sources or the core area of nature reserves;
(2) illegally discharging, dumping, or disposing of hazardous waste in an amount of three tons or more;
(3) discharging, dumping, or disposing of pollutants containing lead, mercury, cadmium, chromium, arsenic, thallium, or antimony, exceeding the national or local pollutant discharge standards by three times or more;
(4) discharging, dumping, or disposing of pollutants containing nickel, copper, zinc, silver, vanadium, manganese, or cobalt, exceeding the national or local pollutant discharge standards by ten times or more;
(5) discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing infectious disease pathogens, or toxic substances by means of evading supervision, such as through underground pipes, seepage wells, seepage pits, fissures, karst caves, or injection;
(6) within two years, having previously been subjected to administrative penalties two or more times for violating national regulations by discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing infectious disease pathogens, or toxic substances, and again committing any of the preceding acts;
(7) key pollutant-discharging units tampering with or falsifying automatic monitoring data, or interfering with automatic monitoring facilities, in the discharge of pollutants such as chemical oxygen demand, ammonia nitrogen, sulfur dioxide, or nitrogen oxides;
(8) illegally reducing the operating expenditure for pollution prevention facilities by one million yuan or more;
(9) illegal gains or causing losses of public or private property of 300,000 yuan or more;
(10) causing serious damage to the ecological environment;
(11) causing interruption of water intake from centralized drinking water sources at or above the township level for twelve hours or more;
(12) causing the loss of basic functions or permanent destruction of five mu or more of basic farmland, shelter forest land, or special-purpose forest land, ten mu or more of other agricultural land, or twenty mu or more of other land;
(13) causing the death of fifty cubic meters or more of forest or other trees, or the death of 2,500 or more young trees;
(14) causing the evacuation or relocation of 5,000 or more people;
(15) causing poisoning of thirty or more people;
(16) causing minor injuries, minor disabilities, or general dysfunction due to organ or tissue damage to three or more people;
(17) causing serious injuries, moderate disabilities, or serious dysfunction due to organ or tissue damage to one or more people;
(18) other circumstances of serious environmental pollution.

Article 3: The conduct prescribed in Articles 338 and 339 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China, under any of the following circumstances, shall be deemed as "particularly serious consequences":
(1) causing interruption of water intake from centralized drinking water sources in urban areas at or above the county level for twelve hours or more;
(2) illegally discharging, dumping, or disposing of hazardous waste in an amount of 100 tons or more;
(3) causing the loss of basic functions or permanent destruction of 15 mu or more of basic farmland, shelter forest land, or special-purpose forest land, 30 mu or more of other agricultural land, or 60 mu or more of other land;
(4) causing the death of 150 cubic meters or more of forest or other trees, or the death of 7,500 or more young trees;
(5) causing losses of public or private property of one million yuan or more;
(6) causing particularly serious damage to the ecological environment;
(7) causing the evacuation or relocation of 15,000 or more people;
(8) causing poisoning of 100 or more people;
(9) causing minor injuries, minor disabilities, or general dysfunction due to organ or tissue damage to ten or more people;
(10) causing serious injuries, moderate disabilities, or serious dysfunction due to organ or tissue damage to three or more people;
(11) causing serious injuries, moderate disabilities, or serious dysfunction due to organ or tissue damage to one or more people, and also causing minor injuries, minor disabilities, or general dysfunction due to organ or tissue damage to five or more people;
(12) causing death or severe disability to one or more people;
(13) other circumstances of particularly serious consequences.

Article 4: Any of the following circumstances in the commission of a criminal act prescribed in Articles 338 and 339 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China shall be given a severe punishment:
(1) obstructing environmental supervision and inspection or investigation of a sudden environmental incident, where the act does not yet constitute a crime such as obstructing public service;
(2) in or near densely populated areas such as hospitals, schools, or residential areas, violating national regulations by discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing infectious disease pathogens, toxic substances, or other hazardous substances;
(3) during the early warning period for heavily polluted weather, during the handling period of a sudden environmental incident, or during the period for making corrections within a prescribed time limit, violating national regulations by discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing infectious disease pathogens, toxic substances, or other hazardous substances;
(4) an enterprise with a hazardous waste operating permit violating national regulations by discharging, dumping, or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing infectious disease pathogens, toxic substances, or other hazardous substances.

Article 10: Where a person, in violation of national regulations, commits any of the following acts against the environmental quality monitoring system, or orders, instructs, or instigates another person to commit any of the following acts, the person shall, in accordance with Article 286 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China, be treated as the crime of destroying a computer information system:
(1) modifying parameters or monitoring data;
(2) interfering with sampling, causing serious distortion of monitoring data;
(3) other acts that damage the environmental quality monitoring system.
Where a key pollutant-discharging unit tampers with or falsifies automatic monitoring data, or interferes with automatic monitoring facilities, and discharges pollutants such as chemical oxygen demand, ammonia nitrogen, sulfur dioxide, or nitrogen oxides, and the act simultaneously constitutes the crime of environmental pollution and the crime of destroying a computer information system, the person shall be convicted and punished in accordance with the provisions providing for a heavier punishment.
Where personnel engaged in the maintenance or operation of environmental monitoring facilities commit or participate in committing acts such as tampering with or falsifying automatic monitoring data, interfering with automatic monitoring facilities, or damaging the environmental quality monitoring system, a severe punishment shall be given.

Article 15: The following substances shall be deemed as "toxic substances" as prescribed in Article 338 of the Criminal Law of the People's Republic of China:
(1) hazardous waste, meaning waste listed in the National Hazardous Waste Inventory, or determined according to the national standards and methods for hazardous waste identification, which has hazardous characteristics;
(2) substances listed in the annexes to the Stockholm Convention on Persistent Organic Pollutants;
(3) pollutants containing heavy metals;
(4) other substances that are toxic and may pollute the environment.
